{% from "macros.j2" import q, plain, question with context %}
<section class="panel" id="tab-decision" data-name="decision">
{{ plain('decision') }}
<h2>Orchestrator decision: targets to test first {{ q('decision') }}</h2>
{{ question('decision') }}
<p class="lede">{{ DEC.rule }} The cards below show, for each chosen gene, the values its list measured, the orchestrator's reasons and the reviewer's verdict with its citations. {{ DEC.n }} genes chosen from a pool of {{ DEC.pool }}.</p>
<div class="sl-legend"><span><i class="lt green"></i> meets</span><span><i class="lt amber"></i> partly</span><span><i class="lt red"></i> fails</span><span><i class="lt grey"></i> not measured</span>
<span><span class="tag ok">reviewer: support</span></span><span><span class="tag warn">reviewer: concerns</span></span><span><span class="tag bad">reviewer: against</span></span></div>
{% for B in DEC.blocks %}
<h3 class="group" id="decision-{{ B.key }}">{{ B.title }}</h3>
<div class="grid">
{% for t in B.cards %}{% set d = t.dossier %}{% set v = t.verdict %}
<div class="card cand sl-card claim" data-evidence="{{ t.evidence_ids | evattr }}">
  <h3>{{ loop.index }}. {{ t.gene }}</h3>
  <div class="meta">
    <span class="tag">group {{ d.group }}{% if d.from_group_b %} (group A had fewer than four){% endif %}</span>
    {% if d.direction %}<span class="tag">{{ d.direction }}</span>{% endif %}
    {% if d.cell_family %}<span class="tag">{{ d.cell_family }}</span>{% elif d.cell_in_single_cells %}<span class="tag">{{ d.cell_in_single_cells }}</span>{% endif %}
    {% if t.category == 'target_and_biomarker' %}<span class="tag b">also a biomarker</span>{% endif %}
    {% if v %}<span class="tag {{ {'support':'ok','concerns':'warn','against':'bad'}[v.verdict] }}">reviewer: {{ v.verdict }}</span>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% if d.lights %}<p class="small">{% for k, L in d.lights.items() %}<span class="nowrap"><i class="lt {{ L.light }}" title="{{ k }}: {{ L.detail }}" aria-label="{{ k }}: {{ L.light }}"></i> {{ k }}</span>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %} {{ d.evidence_ids | cite | safe }}</p>
  <p class="small">{% if d.meta_log2fc is not none %}Meta log2FC {{ d.meta_log2fc }}; {% endif %}{{ d.uc_papers }} UC papers; {{ d.stability }}.{% if d.inhibitor %} Inhibitor: {{ d.inhibitor.drugs | join(", ") }} ({{ d.inhibitor.stage | replace("_", " ") | lower }}){% if d.inhibitor.made_for_cancer %}, made for cancer{% endif %}.{% endif %}</p>
  {% else %}<p class="small">Risk allele {{ d.risk_allele }}: {{ d.direction }}; {{ d.tier }} fine-mapping; predicted effect: {{ d.predicted_effect }}. Biopsies: {{ d.biopsy_change }}. Mendelian randomisation: {{ d.mendelian_randomisation }}. {{ d.drug }}. {{ d.evidence_ids | cite | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
  <p><strong>Why the orchestrator chose it.</strong> {{ t | statement_html | safe }} {{ t.evidence_ids | cite | safe }}</p>
  {% if d.proposed_experiment %}<p class="small"><strong>Proposed first experiment:</strong> {{ d.proposed_experiment }}</p>{% endif %}
  {% if d.key_papers %}<details class="small"><summary>Key papers ({{ d.key_papers | length }})</summary><ul>{% for p in d.key_papers %}<li>{% if p.pmid %}<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/{{ p.pmid }}/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PMID {{ p.pmid }}</a>{% endif %}{% if p.year %} ({{ p.year }}){% endif %}, {{ (p.kind or '') | replace('_', ' ') }}{% if p.direction in ('pathogenic', 'protective') %}, {{ p.direction }}{% endif %}: {{ p.summary }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></details>{% endif %}
  {% if v %}<div class="howbox"><h4>Reviewer{% if DEC.reviewer %} ({{ DEC.reviewer }}){% endif %}: {{ v.verdict }}</h4>{% if v.summary %}<p class="small">{{ v.summary }}</p>{% endif %}
  <ul class="small">{% for r in v.reasons %}<li>{% if r.kind == 'judgement' %}<em>Judgement:</em> {{ r.text }}{% else %}{{ r.text }} <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/{{ r.pmid }}/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PMID {{ r.pmid }}</a>{% if r.journal %} ({{ r.journal }}{% if r.year %}, {{ r.year }}{% endif %}){% endif %}: “{{ r.quote }}” {{ (r.evidence_ids or []) | cite | safe }}{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% if B.not_chosen %}<p class="small"><strong>Not chosen from this list:</strong> {% for r in B.not_chosen %}{{ r.gene }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>{% endif %}
{% for p in (f.narrative.sections.decision or []) if p.list == B.key %}<p class="small claim" data-evidence="{{ p.evidence_ids | evattr }}">{{ p | statement_html | safe }} {{ p.evidence_ids | cite | safe }}</p>{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% if DEC.previous %}<h3>Genes of the earlier selection that left</h3>
<p class="small">Until {{ previous_run }} the orchestrator's selection mixed positive controls, the expected neutrophil signal, new candidates and biomarkers. These genes of that selection are not in the decision pool, and this is where each one is now:</p>
<div class="tw"><table><thead><tr><th>Gene</th><th>Now in</th><th>Why it is not a candidate here</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in DEC.previous %}<tr><td><strong>{{ r.gene }}</strong></td><td>{{ r.now_in }}</td><td>{{ r.reason }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>{% endif %}
<div class="howbox"><h4>How the decision was made and checked</h4><ul>
<li><strong>The pool</strong> is fixed by the data before the orchestrator reads it: group A of each list, the genes that stay among the list's first ten under every way of scoring.</li>
<li><strong>The choice</strong> is the orchestrator's (a language model). Its reasons follow five fixed questions (direction, cell, drug route, safety, first experiment) and every claim cites a record; the reading check and the verifier test them like every other sentence of the atlas.</li>
<li><strong>The rule</strong> (four per list, from the pool, no gene with a drug tried or approved in UC or IBD) is checked by a program{% if verification and verification.decision %}: {{ verification.decision.problems | length }} problems in this run{% endif %}.</li>
<li><strong>The reviewer</strong> is a language model reading as an IBD clinician. Every fact it adds must cite a peer-reviewed paper with a sentence copied from its abstract, checked against PubMed; uncited reasons are discarded. How often it catches errors planted on purpose is measured on the Agent benchmark tab.</li></ul></div>
<div class="note"><strong>How to read this.</strong> These are hypotheses from public data, ranked by evidence and argued by agents; none has been tested as a UC therapy. A green light means a test was met, not that blocking the gene will help patients.</div>
</section>
